research/audit/wave14-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-cex-exponential-not-uniformly-continuous-on-r.result.json:16:  "tail": "ITEM: cex-exponential-not-uniformly-continuous-on-r\nVERDICT: CERTIFIED\nCURRENT-TEXT: READ\nMATHEMATICS: The close pairs have distance tending to 0; MVT, $\\exp'=\\exp$, monotonicity, and exponential growth give image distances tending to $+\\infty$, contradicting uniform continuity. All seven dependencies license their stated uses.\nCITATIONS: [UTSA’s Uniform Continuity notes](https://mathresearch.utsa.edu/wiki/index.php?title=Uniform_Continuity) directly state that $e^x$ is not uniformly continuous on the real line; retained MIT/Lebl sources remain accessible. Removed Keisler support is redundant.\nMETADATA: Dispatch normalized hash matches; provenance ledger is exact-source/literature-derived with AI-altered proof, dependencies match, and no stale `verification.judge` or `audited` stamp remains.\nFINDINGS: NONE"
