research/frontier-6-judge.jsonl-119-{"id":"thm-exponential-limits-and-range","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"[L1] claims exp(x)≥1+x but its source [[def-real-exponential-function-and-e]] only defines the series; the inequality is not stated there and no other justification is provided, so step 1.1 is unsupported.","context_sha256":"0bf7ee90d3204aa74979cd93f9ef51c03b787b54686e3a78f975188f2051d247","at":"2026-07-31T16:30:41.002Z"}
research/frontier-6-judge.jsonl-120-{"id":"lem-scaled-binomial-coefficients-converge","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 1.2 is unlicensed: [L2] gives only algebra of already-known limits, not ι(n)^{-1}→0 (or ι(j)/ι(n)→0). No cited fact establishes this essential limit.","context_sha256":"41d2660e4bb97ce62116c0ebd51e84dea69f18a68e1cccb81534802e823433ef","at":"2026-07-31T16:30:48.073Z"}
research/frontier-6-judge.jsonl-121-{"id":"cor-exponential-reciprocal-and-positivity","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"[L2] asserts squares are nonnegative, but neither lem-of-sign-rules nor def-complete-ordered-field states that; they give product rules and completeness. The step 'so it is nonnegative' relies on an uncertified claim about squares.","context_sha256":"8646ebd29e8c8a06668f848e824ee2a776e49e0ef77d65599b2147cbdae0a0f1","at":"2026-07-31T16:30:50.809Z"}
research/frontier-6-judge.jsonl-122-{"id":"thm-derivative-of-exponential","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"All steps are justified: termwise differentiation applies inside the infinite radius, and the factorial cancellation uses the product representation from def-factorial-and-falling-factorial. Smoothness follows from cor-power-series-sums-are-smooth-with-coefficient-formula. No defect found.","context_sha256":"a67fbae226b690497b3e5cc77daac59c8b7725f286952696ee18464b6fe2d9fe","at":"2026-07-31T16:30:58.934Z"}
research/frontier-6-judge.jsonl:123:{"id":"thm-exponential-product-limit","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 2.1 bounds unweighted coefficient errors, but the finite-head error is \\(\\sum_{k\\le K}|c_{n,k}-1/k!|\\,|x|^k\\). For \\(|x|>1\\), its stated bound does not yield the \\(\\varepsilon/3\\) claim used in 3.1.","context_sha256":"cd39990ff23579e31416a4c87809ebb11bd24102d1d2a2d6d6c4d5d5388280ff","at":"2026-07-31T16:31:11.502Z"}
research/frontier-6-judge.jsonl-124-{"id":"lem-scaled-binomial-coefficients-converge","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"L1 misstates the binomial coefficient formula; the supplied def-binomial-coefficient says the factorial form is a theorem (thm-binomial-closed-formula), not established here. Also, the limit ι(j)/ι(n)→0 in step 1.2 lacks any citation for growth of canonical naturals.","context_sha256":"41d2660e4bb97ce62116c0ebd51e84dea69f18a68e1cccb81534802e823433ef","at":"2026-07-31T16:31:15.306Z"}
research/frontier-6-judge.jsonl-125-{"id":"thm-exponential-ivp-uniqueness","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"Proof correctly applies product and chain rules to get h'=0, then constant-on-interval theorem; all steps are justified by cited facts.","context_sha256":"074268e43e98bd5a2ddb446fa5acd22423d65ea6d4b6d0d74440c5973f27e0c2","at":"2026-07-31T16:31:15.940Z"}
research/frontier-6-judge.jsonl-126-{"id":"thm-exponential-beats-every-polynomial","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"The proof bounds x^m/exp(ax) by C/x via a series term, and C/x→0; all steps rely directly on cited definitions and positivity, with no logical gap.","context_sha256":"e1c97b7c59b57ea9cbb105026f13061d5638d1befabbc1504d3f000ef2cade84","at":"2026-07-31T16:31:20.487Z"}
research/frontier-6-judge.jsonl-127-{"id":"thm-exponential-definition-equivalence","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":null,"reason":"UNPARSEABLE (271 chars): {\"keep\":false,\"reason\":\"[L2] is not a faithful fact statement: it merely names four items and omits their hypotheses and normalizations (e.g. \\(F(1)=e\\), or \\(F(0)=1,F'(0)=1\\)). Thus step 1.1's claim of “exactly the normalization stated here” is unsupported as written.\"}","context_sha256":"902b2942e90fb84850ceb4d207cb9d4d7a7a6268383aee9b01c397140aa9577e","at":"2026-07-31T16:31:23.115Z"}
